to make daily pill taking seem normal and unremarkable. One pill company went so far as to bundle a toothbrush and a bar of soap with each prescription. You know, brush your teeth, wash your face, take your pill, it's kind of, you know, another part of a daily routine. The other challenge that pharmaceutical companies faced as they rolled out this groundbreaking new medication was the conservative outlook of some doctors. In the 1960s, doctors were overwhelmingly male and some were wary about the revolutionary impact the birth control pill would have on sex and general roles.
为了让每日服药看起来正常且毫不起眼。有一家制药公司甚至走得更远，在每份处方中捆绑了一支牙刷和一块香皂。你知道的，刷牙、洗脸、吃药，这有点像你日常生活中的另一个部分。制药公司在推出这款具有划时代意义的新药时面临的另一个挑战是某些医生保守的观点。在20世纪60年代，医生绝大多数是男性，其中一些人对避孕药将对性观念和性别角色产生的革命性影响感到警惕。

