The subject for this afternoon's continuing discussion of the pill is the power to prescribe. In 1967, a group of doctors gathered in San Francisco at a symposium called the Pill and the Puritan Ethic, where they explored the moral implications of the birth control pill. Here's Dr. Donald Minkler, a leader in women's health and family planning, describing the challenges the pill presented for physicians who might be uncomfortable with changing attitudes
