And once again, they used the pill's packaging to help them do that. Pharmaceutical companies produce dozens of ads that targeted physicians. They marketed the new pill packages as a way to help female patients take the pills correctly. They advertise the device as the package that remembers for her or the foolproof method. Each company insisted their pill package design would help the female patients stay on schedule. Which was true, the packaging did help women stay on schedule. But the marketing of these so-called compliance packages played into some doctors' struggles for control at a time when their cultural authority was weakening.
而这一次，他们再次利用避孕药的包装来帮助他们做到这一点。制药公司制作了数十个针对医生的广告。他们将新型药盒作为帮助女性患者正确服药的一种方式进行营销。他们将该装置宣传为“会替她记住的包装”或“万无一失的方法”。每家公司都坚信，他们的药盒设计将有助于女性患者按时服药。这确实是真的，包装确实帮助女性按时服药。但是，对这些所谓的依从性包装的营销，迎合了一些医生在自身文化权威日渐式微之际对控制权的争夺。

